From a0b08c16a8ce49cf4bb2d45caeebccfeb276d7b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 22:12:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 096/187] net: airoha: mark EN7523 OMCI traffic as no-drop

The EN7523 vendor QDMA path sets both the OAM and no-drop bits for OMCI
frames. The current driver sets only the OAM marker, allowing OMCI
traffic to be discarded under queue pressure before the OLT receives a
response.

Set the no-drop bit for xPON OAM frames while preserving the existing
queue, channel, GEM and forward-port fields.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index e9da3b043548..97aa3bf56621 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3460,6 +3460,8 @@ static netdev_tx_t __airoha_dev_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	msg1 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NBOQ_MASK, dev->nbq) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_FPORT_MASK, fport) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_METER_MASK, 0x7f);
+	if (xpon_oam)
+		msg1 |= QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NO_DROP;
 
 	if (xpon)
 		dev_info_ratelimited(&netdev->dev,
-- 
